---
/**
 * Consumer-shadowed /print page.
 *
 * The scaffold's print integration assumes single-book consumers AND
 * uses the default MDX component context (without our custom AnkiCard,
 * NarrativeBox, etc). For the multi-book corpus we redirect readers to
 * per-book Paged.js export pages (one PDF per book), which will be
 * implemented post-Phase-1.
 *
 * TODO(scaffold-v3.2): allow scaffold print route to accept a
 * `components` prop. Issue filed upstream.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Print exports" description="Print-friendly book exports">
  <h1>Print Exports</h1>
  <p>
    Print-friendly PDF exports are generated per book via Paged.js. Multi-book
    print mode is pending Phase 1 acceptance.
  </p>
  <p>
    For now, visit individual books and use your browser's <code>Print &rarr; Save as PDF</code>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/knowledge-graphs-rag/">Knowledge Graphs for RAG</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>
